ure, but the primary complaint is headache"], "alarm_features": ["severe hypertension", "confusion", "acute severe headache"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Vascular Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5070422535211268, "posterior": 0.4638880050906778, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The patient's sudden severe headache, confusion, and severely elevated blood pressure suggest a possible vascular disorder such as a hemorrhagic stroke. The symptoms of headache, confusion, and fever could be indicative of an infectious disorder such as meningitis, but the patient's presentation and medical history are more suggestive of a vascular disorder. A CT of the head is the most appropriate initial imaging test to determine the cause of the symptoms and guide further management."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Have you experienced any recent head trauma?", "Do you have a history of hypertension?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["CT of the head", "MRI of the head"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Infectious Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "prior": 0.2535211267605633, "posterior": 0.11454024817053769, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The patient's sudden severe headache, confusion, and severely elevated blood pressure suggest a possible vascular disorder such as a hemorrhagic stroke. The symptoms of headache, confusion, and fever could be indicative of an infectious disorder such as meningitis, but the patient's presentation and medical history are more suggestive of a vascular d